# Storybook gate

- Any **new UI element** (component, primitive, layout pattern) must have a Storybook story added or updated before it is committed.
- Mid-iteration visual tweaks while coding do not require a Storybook round-trip on every keystroke — but **before each commit** that touches UI sources, Storybook must reflect the committed UI.
- UI sources include: `components/**`, `app/**/*.tsx` (presentational pieces), `stories/**`, and theme tokens in `app/globals.css`.
- Place stories next to components (`*.stories.tsx`) or under `stories/foundation/` for tokens / typography.
- Run `npm run storybook` locally to verify. Pre-commit hook reminds when UI files change without Storybook file changes.
